From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Compare the requested scale to the maximum width as signed

The requested scale is an int32_t, read from a constant argument, and
Decimal::MAX_WIDTH_INT128 is unsigned, so -Wsign-compare flags the comparison.
The width is cast to int32_t, which holds it exactly, after the negative case
has been ruled out by the same condition.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/operator/decimal_division.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/operator/decimal_division.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/operator/decimal_division.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/operator/decimal_division.cpp
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@
 	if (input.GetArgumentCount() == 3) {
 		auto scale_val = input.GetNonNullConstant(2);
 		auto scale_i = scale_val.GetValue<int32_t>();
-		if (scale_i < 0 || scale_i > Decimal::MAX_WIDTH_INT128) {
+		if (scale_i < 0 || scale_i > static_cast<int32_t>(Decimal::MAX_WIDTH_INT128)) {
 			throw InvalidInputException("decimal_division: scale must be between 0 and %d, got %d",
 			                            Decimal::MAX_WIDTH_INT128, scale_i);
 		}
